.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1025 AM PDT Wed Sep 30 2026

Developing marine layer is battling building high pressure over
the region. As such, the inversion height is compressed leading to
low CIGs along the coast. That being said, expecting VFR through
early this evening. CIGs return early for MRY/SNS and later for N
Bay and in SF Bay. Moderate conf for fog development tonight given
the shallow nature of the marine layer.

Vicinity of SFO...VRF through this evening. CIGs slowly redevelop
inside SF Bay impacting OAK and SFO 07-09Z timeframe. Lower CIGs
linger into the AM rush for Thursday.

SFO Bridge Approach...Less chc for late night CIGs, but still
expecting some around the approach zone.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR through this afternoon, but CIGs
lurking outside of MRY Bay will return early this evening. High
conf on fog impacts by Thursday morning.

