.MARINE...
(Today through Monday)
Issued at 1025 AM PDT Wed Sep 30 2026

Northerly winds will continue to ease through the day, but still
hazardous with moderate to strong breezes. Strongest winds are
over the outer waters north of Point Reyes. Conditions will
improve later this week and weekend as northwesterly breezes
diminish to become gentle to moderate. Rough to very rough seas
today will subside to moderate by Friday.

